<h1>Facility Operations, Readings &amp; Logs, PPM</h1>
<p class="story-lead">A fast-growing co-working operator had no clear view of what was happening across its campuses. FusionEdge gave every campus the same processes, tracked 32,000+ assets, and measured electricity by time of day so tenants are billed for what they use.</p>
<ul>
<li>14 campuses in 6 cities on one standard way of working</li>
<li>32,000+ assets tracked</li>
<li>PPM tasks done on time: 52% to 96%</li>
<li>Unplanned breakdowns down 45%</li>
<li>Cleaning checklist compliance: 61% to 95%</li>
<li>18% more electricity cost recovered from tenants</li>
<li>Overall energy cost down 12%</li>
<li>Time to set up a new campus: 3 weeks to 5 days</li>
<li>Rollout time: 10 weeks</li>
</ul>
<h2>The client and the challenge</h2>
<p>The client runs co-working spaces across India. Tenants pay for a space that simply works: clean desks, cool air, working lifts, and steady power. Delivering that every day needs visibility of what is happening at every campus, reliability of every AC, DG set, lift, and pump, and a record of who did what and when so costs can be controlled.</p>
<p>The client had none of these across its campuses. As it opened new locations, equipment broke down and the central team often did not know. Each campus had its own cleaning schedule and its own way of working. There was no single SOP, and electricity used by tenants after office hours was not measured, so the operator paid for it.</p>
<p>The operator wanted every campus, old and new, to work the same way before it expanded further.</p>
<h2>What we found</h2>
<ul>
<li>14 different cleaning and maintenance routines. Every campus worked its own way.</li>
<li>52% of PPM tasks were done on time. Almost half of planned maintenance was late or missed.</li>
<li>1 in 3 breakdowns was reported to the central team. Most issues were fixed, or not, without anyone knowing.</li>
<li>100% of meter readings were taken on paper. There was no live view of electricity use.</li>
<li>0% of tenant power use after 9 pm was billed. Extra-hours electricity was a hidden loss.</li>
</ul>
<h2>The solution</h2>
<p>FusionEdge was rolled out to all 14 campuses in 10 weeks, in four steps.</p>
<ul>
<li>One standard for every campus. The same SOPs, cleaning schedules, and digital checklists were set up across all campuses. A new campus now goes live in 5 days using the same template.</li>
<li>Every asset on one system. 32,000+ assets, including ACs, DG sets, UPS, lifts, and pumps, were added with their service history.</li>
<li>PPM that actually happens. Planned maintenance schedules were loaded for every asset. Technicians get reminders on their phone, and each task is closed with a photo as proof.</li>
<li>Electricity tracked by time of day. Using Readings &amp; Logs, meters are read at set times, including the 9 am to 9 pm working window. The operator can see which tenant used how much power, and when, and bill extra-hours use correctly.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Before and after</h2>
<ul>
<li>How campuses work: 14 different routines, replaced by one standard SOP.</li>
<li>Breakdowns: often unknown to the central team, then every breakdown logged and tracked, with 45% fewer.</li>
<li>Planned maintenance: 52% done on time, then 96% done on time with photo proof.</li>
<li>Cleaning: different schedules and 61% checklist compliance, then the same schedule everywhere and 95% compliance.</li>
<li>Electricity readings: on paper, once a day or less, then digital readings at fixed times through the day.</li>
<li>Extra-hours power: not measured and not billed, then measured and billed to the right tenant.</li>
<li>New campus setup: about 3 weeks, then 5 days.</li>
</ul>
<p>Spotting energy spikes early, and fixing the equipment behind them, cut overall energy cost by 12%.</p>
<h2>The five outcomes</h2>
<ul>
<li>Standardization. All 14 campuses follow the same SOPs, cleaning schedules, and checklists.</li>
<li>Savings. 18% more electricity cost recovered from tenants, and 12% lower energy bills.</li>
<li>Energy insight. A live view of power use by time of day, with spikes flagged early.</li>
<li>Reliable PPM. 96% of planned maintenance done on time, and 45% fewer breakdowns.</li>
<li>Evidence and quality. Every task is closed with a photo and time stamp, so service quality can be proven to tenants.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Modules used</h2>
<ul>
<li>Asset Management, for every asset and its service history</li>
<li>Preventive Maintenance, for PPM schedules with reminders and photo proof</li>
<li>Readings &amp; Logs, for electricity and equipment readings at set times</li>
<li>Digital Checklists, for the same cleaning and SOP checklists at every campus</li>
<li>Executive Dashboard, for one view of all campuses</li>
</ul>
